From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lousberg <25581128+p0nti@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:12:11 +0100
Subject: fix: refresh X11 keyboard mappings on XKB map changes

Partially backport Chromium f9e103beb9c505ee81424b81f7b652eb67b33691
by Thomas Anderson (https://crrev.com/c/8778792). Include only its
XKB event classification, subscription and cached-keymap refresh fixes,
without the navigator.keyboard.getLayoutMap() feature changes.

Without map notifications an XKB type update can leave a keypad key
reported as ArrowDown while NumLock is on and its character is 2.
This was reproduced in Electron 42.11.18 with and without Xpra.

Add raw-wire regression coverage for all twelve XKB event subtypes,
synthetic events and an unknown subtype. Also verify that a map
notification refreshes cached keysyms after a server-side mapping update.

This patch can be removed when Electron updates to Chromium containing
f9e103beb9c505ee81424b81f7b652eb67b33691.

